      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Knee pain and injury are commonly seen in children and adolescents. A comprehensive evaluation of the knee is built on an appreciation of the anatomy, biomechanics, and pathophysiology of common disorders. This article considers these issues and describes a sequential technique for physical examination of the knee. Relevant imaging options and management strategies also are discussed."},
